# A4 step 6: modules/status/README.md documents the module.
# Names must appear as the first cell of a table row (| name |), not just anywhere.
modules/status/README.md | ^# [^#[:space:]] | must start with a title: one # and a space, then the name (## is a subheading, not a title)
modules/status/README.md | ^##+ .*Requirements | needs a "Requirements" section
modules/status/README.md | ^##+ .*Inputs | needs an "Inputs" section
modules/status/README.md | ^##+ .*Outputs | needs an "Outputs" section
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?archive`? *\| | needs a Requirements row for the archive provider
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?project_name`? *\| | needs a table row for the project_name input
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?table_name`? *\| | needs a table row for the table_name input
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?table_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the table_arn input
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?api_id`? *\| | needs a table row for the api_id input
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?api_execution_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the api_execution_arn input
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?status_role_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the status_role_arn output
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?status_function_name`? *\| | needs a table row for the status_function_name output
modules/status/README.md | ^\| *`?status_route_key`? *\| | needs a table row for the status_route_key output
